  "id": "COMPOUND:12208 - PROTEIN:1722",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between the Influenza B virus B/Hong Kong/259/2010 hemagglutinin antigen and the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit rho-3. All three paths indicate that the hemagglutinin antigen acts as a target for Magnesium levulinate, which in turn targets the receptor subunit rho-3. This suggests a potential pathway where the hemagglutinin antigen is indirectly involved in the regulation of the receptor subunit rho-3 through the intermediary of Magnesium levulinate. The shared involvement of Magnesium levulinate in all three paths implies a common mechanism, possibly related to its role as a modulator of receptor activity. The evidence supports a hypothesis that the hemagglutinin antigen may influence the receptor subunit rho-3 via a pathway involving Magnesium levulinate, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
